## Custom vm.args for Glorbo — generated by Mix Release, consumed by Burrito.
##
## Burrito's erlang_launcher.zig bypasses bin/<release> and invokes erlexec
## directly with `-args_file releases/<vsn>/vm.args` (see
## deps/burrito/src/erlang_launcher.zig ~L55-73). `rel/env.sh.eex` is dead
## code under Burrito — node-distribution flags MUST live here.
##
## The `-setcookie` value is sourced from the `RELEASE_COOKIE` env var
## (honoured by Burrito at erlang_launcher.zig ~L44). `glorbo up` exports
## it from `Glorbo.Config.erl_cookie/1` when spawning the daemon.
##
## DISTRIBUTION IS NOT STARTED HERE. Earlier revisions pinned
## `-name glorbo@127.0.0.1` so the daemon would be remsh-addressable
## from `glorbo console`. That produced the following papercut: any
## second ./glorbo invocation — even `./glorbo help` — tried to
## register the same node name and collided with the running daemon,
## failing BEAM-startup before Elixir code got a chance to print a
## useful error ("Protocol 'inet_tcp': the name glorbo@127.0.0.1
## seems to be in use by another Erlang node"). Distribution is now
## started programmatically from Elixir (see
## `Glorbo.CLI.Lifecycle.Distribution.start/0`) only for the verbs
## that actually need it (serve, up, console). Help / status /
## down / doctor / reindex / new-* / import-* never touch EPMD.
##
## Listener bound to an ephemeral port (kernel 0/0) so a running
## daemon never pins a predictable port in another BEAM's way.
-kernel inet_dist_listen_min 0
-kernel inet_dist_listen_max 0
